# Live tuning overlay

The shell is a menu bar, a navigator, an inspector, an optional help column, and a timeline strip. Help is an ImGui column beside the inspector. It does not cover the visualiser. Width is an editor preference. Session state becomes view state; inspector pages come from section defs in `row_sections.py`. Toasts are an ImGui top-layer window in the visualiser corner. `RowLayout` no longer draws them. Overlay Latin text uses bundled DejaVu Sans Mono; icons use Material Icons in `assets/fonts/`.

## Where new fields go

A new field is an inspector group child or a command. Groups are built from `row_sections.py`:

- Settings: `SETTINGS_SECTION`
- Project: `PROJECT_SECTION`
- Layers: `TRACK_SECTION` (preset curation uses `CURATION_LAYER_SECTION`)
- Overlays, Post-FX, and pattern mask: `RENDER_OVERLAYS_SECTION`, `RENDER_POST_FX_SECTION`, `RENDER_PATTERN_MASK_SECTION`
- Timeline preset, beat / bar grid, and cue fades: `TIMELINE_PRESETS_SECTION`, `BEAT_BAR_GRID_SECTION`, `TIMELINE_CUTS_SECTION`
- Song markers: `SONG_MARKERS_SECTION`

Open and closed state is an `InspectorGroupKey` on the shell (`collapsed` and `opened`). There is no session `expanded` flag for a group. Cleave effects, beat / bar grid, and cue fades start closed. A closed group hides its children.

Conditional rows are siblings shown or hidden by a value predicate. They have no arrow and no open/closed key. The view-state structure includes or omits them at build time and rebuilds only when `view_state_structure_signature()` changes. A field that gates row presence belongs in that signature; leave value-only fields out. Add a `test_structure_signature_invalidates_on_*` test in `tests/cleave/viz/test_view_state_structure.py`.

New rows use `RowKind`, `RowSpec`, and `SectionNode`. Do not add a per-`RowKind` label or mutation branch in `tuning_panel_draw.py` or `controls.py`. Overlay chrome lives in `overlay_primitives`. Timeline, help, and modal must not import `tuning_panel_draw`. `render_visibility_icon` stays in `row_present_renderers.py`.

The timeline strip stays its own host in `timeline_overlay.py`. Cue blocks are edited on the strip, not in the inspector. Do not fold the strip into `RowLayout`.

## Parameterized actions

When an action needs parameters, keep the inspector row as a plain `ACTION` line. On Enter, chain one modal per parameter, then apply.

Exception: timeline preset parameters live as child value rows in the timeline preset group. Apply confirms with Yes/Cancel and lists staged choices as `labeled_lines`.

## Render enabled

`enabled=False` on a render header must skip that block in the frame path, not only dim the inspector row. Overlay cards gate per card. Post-FX children must check `session.render_post_fx.enabled`. New post-FX subsections need an `enabled=False` test.

## Typography

Colors live in `cleave/viz/theme.py`. Use existing roles (`LABEL`, `VALUE`, `ACTION`, `DISABLED`, `LOCKED`) plus the accent constants already there. Do not invent a new color without adding a theme constant.

Label+value rows: prefix in `LABEL`, value in the row value color. Expand arrows use the value role. Exceptions (single-color action rows, settings and project headers, transport, notifications, modals) are deliberate; match nearby rows.

## Keyboard dispatch

Layered in `input_dispatch.py`. Modal keys first. Then Tab / Shift+Tab cycles Menu, Navigator, Inspector, Help, and Timeline. Help is skipped when the column is closed. Timeline is skipped when the strip is closed. Then the menu bar, command shortcuts, and Ctrl+Up / Ctrl+Down (previous / next top-level navigator node; no effect while the menu bar is focused). Navigator and inspector own their arrows, Enter, Esc, and PageUp/PageDown. An open strip does not take keys. Timeline takes arrows, Enter, Esc, and cue keys only while that region is active. `h` toggles the help column and stays global. Opening help does not move focus. Esc while Help is focused closes the column and restores the previous stop. It does not hide the UI. There is no panel region and no main-list focus ring.

`row_hotkeys.handle_row_hotkey` is the per-descriptor path for letter, Delete, and Backspace keys, used by the navigator and the inspector.
